{"repositoryId":1217217809,"availability":"available","full":"tiw302/iso-deployment-bot","name":"iso-deployment-bot","description":"Automated ISO mirroring system that syncs OS images to Google Drive and generates a static web directory for browsing and downloading.","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-21T17:00:29Z","updated":"2026-10-15T20:23:43Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://tiw302.github.io/iso-deployment-bot/","topics":["aria2","automation","dashboard","github-actions","github-pages","homelab","iso-mirror","proxmox","python","rclone"],"demo":"https://tiw302.github.io/iso-deployment-bot/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:30.818Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:30.818Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:30.818Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T22:40:30.818Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A simple, automated ISO mirroring system for homelabs and personal use. This project utilizes an ephemeral runner architecture via GitHub Actions, fetching operating system images through multi-threaded downloaders (aria2c) and synchronizing them directly to Google Drive (rclone) to generate a static web directory.","os-deployment-library (OSDL) is a modest collection of Python scripts designed to automate the downloading and storing of operating system ISOs.","It was built as a practical workaround for homelab operators or developers who frequently need to provision virtual machines but find it inconvenient to repeatedly download images from slow or distant official mirrors. By utilizing GitHub Actions as a free compute runner and Rclone to upload files to Google Drive, it maintains a personal repository of OS images with minimal manual intervention."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tiw302/iso-deployment-bot/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"17d5726c6bdd796a63f669c131b402e2b3dfeb827221bba7